                    "Landscape photography and Lightroom editing, running since July 2016.  <mark>333,000 subscribers</mark>, 474 videos, <mark>34,219,192 lifetime views</mark>.  Every Wednesday without a gap, which matters later because it rules out the easy explanation.",
                    "The numbers.  Across his last ten uploads, 26 August to 28 October, the <mark>median is 44,725 views</mark>, from a middle pair of 41,479 and 47,970.  Across the previous ten, 17 June to 19 August, the <mark>median is 20,011</mark>, from a middle pair of 15,915 and 24,106.  That is <mark>2.24 times</mark>.  The median is the right measure because the recent block holds a 140,285 outlier that would flatter an average, and the floor moved too: his weakest recent video did <mark>28,104</mark>, which is 1.4 times the earlier median and beats seven of the previous ten outright.",
                    "The turn is datable to <mark>7 October</mark>, and three things changed on the same upload.  First the subject narrowed: every video since is a single-technique editing walkthrough, one thing at a time, where the earlier blocks mixed gear talk, camera-setting philosophy and software news.  Second the runtime locked into a band, 11 minutes 31 to 12 minutes 31 across four uploads, where the earlier block ran anywhere from under 10 minutes to over 15 with no pattern.  Third, and this is the one nobody notices, the descriptions were gutted.  His 30 September video carries twelve outbound links across twenty lines.  His 7 October video carries one link in four lines.  Every upload since follows the short version.",
                    "The result is not subtle.  The two biggest videos of his last twenty, <mark>140,285 and 105,229</mark>, both arrive after 7 October, and the four uploads since that date have a higher median than the ten before them.  Cadence did not change, so the usual explanation is off the table.  What changed is what a viewer is promised when they click and how much clutter they meet when they arrive.",
                    "There is no sponsor, and the gap is recent and datable.  Squarespace ran as a recurring integration through 24 June, 15 July, 22 July, 5 August and 12 August, then stopped.  A Luminar promotion ran on 26 August.  DxO PhotoLab 10 ran on 23 September.  Since 7 October, nothing.  Reading the full descriptions of his five most recent videos, every outbound link is his own: a free course, two of his own guides, a paid course on Gumroad, plus the older-style video's affiliate links to a camera retailer and his own workshop and gear pages.  No promotion codes for anybody else, no thanks to any sponsor.  So the slot has been empty across his four best-performing videos of the year, and there is no incumbent to displace.",
